# Project conventions

- Use Vite and vanilla strict TypeScript. Do not add a UI framework.
- Keep the site static and mobile-first. Deploy it to GitHub Pages at `https://xgrybvo6508-dot.github.io/vladislav-card/`.
- Set Vite `base` to `/vladislav-card/`. Build asset URLs from `import.meta.env.BASE_URL`; do not assume the domain root.
- Put all editable public profile copy and structured facts in exactly one file: `src/content/profile.ts`. UI and chat code consume that data; do not duplicate profile facts elsewhere.
- Use `vitest`, ESLint, and Prettier. Keep these npm scripts: `dev`, `build`, `test`, `lint`, and `typecheck`.

# Layout

```text
src/
  main.ts       # bootstrap only
  content/      # profile.ts: single content source of truth
  ui/           # semantic views, dialogs, and CSS
  chat/         # settings, grounded prompt, OpenAI-compatible client
  lib/          # small pure helpers and boundary validation
public/         # local static assets, including the generated OG PNG
```

- Colocate tests as `*.test.ts`.
- Use ES modules and named exports. Avoid `any`; validate `unknown` at API and localStorage boundaries.
- Keep pure logic DOM-free and inject fetch/storage where useful for testing.
- Do not use third-party fonts, CDNs, trackers, analytics, or runtime dependencies that send data unexpectedly.
- Before calling work complete, run `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, and `npm run build`.
